    "message": "feat(mcp): add ix mcp subcommand exposing the code graph as MCP tools (#219)\r\n\r\nRuns a dual-era MCP stdio server (2026-07-28 stateless + 2025-06-18\r\ninitialize handshake) exposing seven read-only tools bound to\r\nmap/status/explain/trace/impact/search/rank and reusing --format llm.\r\nTool arguments are validated against per-tool JSON schemas and executed\r\nvia the F-010 execFile pattern (no shell, hard timeout, kill on\r\nnotifications/cancelled). Registered in oss.ts with a regression guard\r\nmirroring the F-009 discipline (89ca55e); no Pro stub can shadow it.\r\nThe remap write tool is intentionally absent — /__ix/remap does not\r\nexist on this base (added by the unmerged hardening PR).\r\n\r\n34 new tests: protocol/validation units, in-memory dual-era session,\r\nregistration guard, and a real-process stdio integration test.",
